    d: 'Clonorchis sinensis, the Chinese liver fluke, is diagnosed by finding its eggs in stool or duodenal aspirate, not routinely by liver biopsy.',
    e: 'Since Fasciola hepatica, Fasciola gigantica and Clonorchis sinensis are all diagnosed by egg examination rather than liver biopsy, "all of the above" is incorrect; liver biopsy applies specifically to the tissue-migrating Toxocara larva.',
